PATCH 342 -- FUN_0000_6980 (the NovaLogic Voxel-Space column raycaster, the mission-windshield TERRAIN
colour producer): model its self-modifying projection lookup faithfully + rebase its un-based in-image
data references, so the port's real 6980 runs to completion and reads the correct proj/ramp/matrix data
instead of dereferencing wild host addresses (SIGSEGV).  This is the PROJ-SMC-MODEL fix from
docs/oracle_colour_gate.md + docs/oracle_6980_colour_proof.md.  Mission-path only (6980 is never reached
by the 25 menu/intro/settings verify flows); default boot unaffected.

THE DEFECTS (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin @ ext 0x6980..0x6bf6, x86:LE:32 flat PM):

  6a04: mov ds:0x6add,eax   ; eax = ds:0x3909 (proj base ptr) with al := -(90dc>>25) (=L0 shade base)
        -> the SMC operand of `mov eax,IMM32` at 6adc is patched to  (projptr & 0xffffff00) | L0
  6adc: mov eax,0x7fffffff  ; RELOADS the (SMC-patched) IMM each depth; middle word inc'd +0x100/depth
  6aeb: add al,[esi+ecx]    ; al := (L0 + heightmap[coord]) & 0xff
  6aee: mov al,[eax]        ; sy = proj[ (projptr & 0xffffff00) + d*0x100 + ((L0+h)&0xff) ]

Ghidra could not model the SMC, so it emitted the STATIC forms:
  * `_uRam00006add = CONCAT31((uint)LAB_0000_3909 >> 8, L0)` -- LAB_0000_3909 is (after the FLAT32
    assemble) a BYTE deref of [0x3909], not the 32-bit proj-pointer VALUE `mov eax,ds:0x3909`.
  * `bVar3 = *(byte*)CONCAT31(0x7fffff, hm[coord] + -1)` -- the un-patched 0x7fffffff immediate (low
    byte 0xff -> the `-1`) instead of the SMC-patched base + (L0+h) index.  A wild deref -> SIGSEGV.
The per-depth SMC advance (inc word[6ade]/[6b5e]) is ALREADY modelled (the two `sRam*+1` stores).

Additionally 6980 has three un-based in-image data references the FLAT32 assemble left as bare host
literals (Ghidra emitted raw constants, not &DAT/&FUN symbols) -> they read host 0x9454/0x4224/0x4624
(unmapped) instead of ext_base+off:
  6a72: mov ecx,[edi*4+0x4624]   (4624 ramp)   ; 6a94: mov ecx,[edi*4+0x4224]   (4224 ramp)
  69be: mov eax,[ebx+... 0x9454] (sin/cos matrix, sibling of the based &FUN_0000_944b+5 read at 0x9450)

THE FIX (faithful, control-flow 1:1):
  * SMC init: read the 32-bit proj-pointer VALUE at [0x3909] (host ptr, 0x100-aligned) into the operand.
  * SMC lookup (both colour columns): sy = *(byte*)( (op & 0xffffff00) | (byte)((byte)op + hm[coord]) )
    where op = _uRam00006add (fwd col) / _uRam00006b5d (rev col); op advances +0x100 per depth already.
  * rebase the three bare in-image reads to g_mem + fist_ext_base + off.

NB the proj table [0x3909] must be 0x100-aligned (the SMC masks the operand low byte); the port's
allocator FUN_0000_36bf (13091: 36bf(...,&LAB_0000_3909,0x100,0x8536)) must return 0x100-aligned when
the op-0x24 wiring lands (verify next iteration).  PROVEN standalone: FIST_6980PROVE (tools/native_main.c)
feeds the frame-matched capture (0x100-aligned proj) + this patch -> the port's real 6980 reproduces the
oracle 6980 shadow (see docs/oracle_6980_colour_proof.md for the exact byte-match).

